      "writtenOn": "2024-06-17T11:47:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @yiyishen@google.com\n\nA 1: Broadcast stop is called from upper layers - there is no such logic to stop broadcast and do handover unicast.\nA 2: Yes this is the expected behavior - I thought we agreed on that 😊 there are two steps inside this solution:\n a) Broadcast stop: means that user must agree/application decides to not broadcast audio - why it should broadcast if intention is to switch to classic.\n b) change active/fallback LE Audio device to null - this is basically a normal procedure for changing active device. Changing LE Audio device to null should always result in no fallback device and/or current active device.\n \nFeel free if something is not clear ;)\n\nRegards,\nGrzegorz",
      "parentUuid": "1ad1a470_507f3242",
      "revId": "3996a0cfc2ab32b4923824f842138ac630c65a5d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
